### useTxFormField

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| `useTxFormField` | `(kind?: 'input' \| 'button' \| 'group') => TxFormField \| null` | Connects a control to the item around it; `kind` decides how the label names the control. Returns `null` outside a form. |
| `id` | `string \| undefined` | Read-only; the id the label points at. Only the first control in an item receives one. |
| `labelId` / `label` | `string \| undefined` / `string` | Read-only; the id and text of the item's label. |
| `describedBy` | `string \| undefined` | Read-only; the id of the message or help text. |
| `invalid` / `required` | `boolean` | Read-only; an error is showing; the field is required. |
| `disabled` / `size` | `boolean` / `'sm' \| 'md' \| 'lg'` | Read-only; the form's `disabled` and `size`. |
| `attrs` | `(host?: Record<string, unknown>) => Record<string, unknown>` | The control's merged attributes; those the control was given win, except `aria-describedby`, which keeps both. |

### provideTxFormHost

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| `provideTxFormHost` | `(host: TxFormHost, app?: App) => void` | Gives the forms below — or, with `app`, in the whole app — what the host decides. Call it in a component's `setup`. |
| `host.messages` | `MaybeRefOrGetter<Partial<FormMessages>>` | Text in the host's language; a ref or getter follows locale switches. |
| `host.namespace` | `MaybeRefOrGetter<string \| null>` | Whose drafts these are, as `user:42`; `null` until that is known, and no draft is kept meanwhile. |
| `host.storage` | `FormDraftStorage` | Where drafts go when `persist.storage` does not say. |
| `host.leaveConfirm` | `FormLeaveConfirm` | Asks before leaving, for the forms without their own `leaveConfirm`. |
| `flushTxForms` | `() => Promise<void>` | Writes every mounted form's pending draft, before the page goes without warning. |
| `clearTxFormDrafts` | `(options?: { namespace?: string, storage?: FormDraftStorage }) => Promise<void>` | Removes the drafts, or one namespace's. |

### Types

`FormRule`, one entry of `rules`:

| Field | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `required` | `boolean` | Rejects empty values. |
| `type` | `'email' \| 'url' \| 'number' \| 'integer'` | The value's format. |
| `min` / `max` | `number` | Numeric range. |
| `minLength` / `maxLength` | `number` | Characters in a string, or items in an array. |
| `pattern` | `RegExp` | A pattern the value must match. |
| `message` | `string` | Message when this rule fails, replacing the built-in text. |
| `level` | `'error' \| 'warning'` | `warning` shows its message but never blocks submit. |
| `deps` | `string[]` | Fields whose edits re-check this one while it shows a message. |
| `validator` | `(value, rule, model, { signal, path }) => boolean \| string \| Promise<boolean \| string>` | Return `false` or a message to fail; declare it `async` when it awaits. |

`FormReconcileContext`, the argument of `reconcile`; every value is a copy, free to change:

| Field | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `source` | `'baseline' \| 'draft'` | `baseline` is `setBaseline()`; `draft` is a stored draft whose fields were saved again since. |
| `incoming` | `FormValues` | The values arriving; they become the new baseline whatever `model` ends up holding. |
| `current` | `FormValues` | `model` as the user left it. |
| `baseline` | `FormValues` | The baseline the user's edits were made against. |
| `dirtyPaths` | `string[]` | Paths the user changed that `incoming` also carries. |
| `merged` | `FormValues` | The default, taken when nothing is returned: `incoming` with `dirtyPaths` kept, or for a draft, `model` as it is. |
| `origin` | `FormValues` | For a draft: the saved values its edits were made against, for a three-way merge. |

`FormPersistOptions`, the object form of `persist`:

| Field | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `recordId` | `string \| number` | Keeps each record's draft apart: `42` for `/posts/42/edit`. |
| `namespace` | `string` | Whose drafts these are; defaults to the host's, then `default`. |
| `version` | `number` | Bump it when the model's shape changes; a draft from another version is dropped. Default `1`. |
| `ttl` | `number \| '7d' \| '12h' \| '30m'` | How long a draft lasts after its last write, in milliseconds or units. Default `'7d'`. |
| `storage` | `'local' \| 'session' \| 'memory' \| FormDraftAdapter` | Defaults to the host's, then `local`; `memory` lasts until the page reloads. |
| `exclude` | `string[]` | Paths never written, on top of the secret fields. |
| `restore` | `'auto' \| 'manual'` | `manual` waits for the notice or `restoreDraft()`. Default `auto`. |

`FormDraftAdapter`, a store of your own; every method may return a promise:

| Field | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `get` / `remove` | `(key: string) => string \| null` / `(key: string) => void` | Reads or deletes one draft. |
| `set` | `(key: string, value: string) => void` | Throw when the value was not stored; the form keeps it in memory meanwhile. |
| `clear` | `(prefix: string) => void` | Optional; removes the keys starting with `prefix`, for `clearTxFormDrafts()`. |

`FormMessages`, the built-in text; the English defaults are `FORM_DEFAULT_MESSAGES`:

| Field | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `required` / `invalid` / `pattern` | `(label: string) => string` | Missing value, failed validator, mismatched pattern. |
| `type` | `(label: string, type: FormRuleType) => string` | Wrong `type`. |
| `min` / `max` | `(label: string, limit: number) => string` | Out of the numeric range. |
| `minLength` / `maxLength` | `(label: string, limit: number, unit: 'characters' \| 'items') => string` | Out of the length range. |
| `field` | `string` | Stands in for the name when an item has neither `label` nor `prop`. |
| `errorPrefix` / `warningPrefix` | `string` | Read before an error or a warning; hidden on screen. |
| `validating` | `string` | Shown when an async check runs past one second. |
| `optional` | `string` | After optional labels when `requiredMark="optional"`. |
| `summaryTitle` | `string` | Default heading of `TxFormErrorSummary`. |
| `draftRestored` / `draftPending` | `(savedAt: Date) => string` | The notice once a draft has filled the form in, or while it waits. |
| `draftRestore` / `draftDiscard` | `string` | The notice's buttons. |
| `leaveConfirm` | `string` | Asked through `window.confirm` when nothing else asks. |

